{'symbol': 'BALL', 'date': '2022-07-28 09:35:00', 'title': 'BALL AEROSPACE SELECTED FOR TWO NOAA WEATHER INSTRUMENT STUDIES', 'text': "ONE INSTRUMENT DESIGN WOULD MEASURE ATMOSPHERIC COMPOSITION THE OTHER OCEAN COLOR BROOMFIELD, COLO., JULY 28, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- IN A ONE-WEEK PERIOD, BALL AEROSPACE WAS SELECTED BY NASA TO COMPLETE TWO 20-MONTH STUDIES ON NEW INSTRUMENTS TO SUPPORT THE NATIONAL OCEANIC AND ATMOSPHERIC ADMINISTRATION'S (NOAA'S) GEOSTATIONARY EXTENDED OBSERVATIONS (GEOXO) PROGRAM: ONE TO MEASURE ATMOSPHERIC COMPOSITION (ACX) AND ONE TO MEASURE OCEAN COLOR (OCX)."}